7.2.6.m:
With: "Indra indeed the singers...", from the eastern half; with: "You are held by a support; for Indra accompanied by the Arka...", he draws it. With: "This is your womb; for Indra accompanied by the Arka...", he sets it down. With: "To you, O hero, we shout...", on the southern half; with: "You indeed we invoke...", on the northern half;

"Now may we accomplish these worlds, / Indra and all the gods;

and our sacrifice, our body, and our offspring / may Indra accomplish together with the Ādityas!"

"That indeed was the eldest in the worlds, / whence the fierce one of glittering valor was born;

as soon as born he crushes the enemies, / after whom all the helpers rejoice,"

7.2.7.m:
Eight female servants carrying water-jars, wearing striking garments, two by two around the mārjālīya hearth,

"Cows alone are fragrant, / cows have the fragrance of bdellium;

cows are the mothers of clarified butter; / let them be numerous here!"

—thus they sing; stamping their feet with: "This is madhūka honey!", they circumambulate clockwise.

"The cows of Maṅgīra indeed / did not drink the water of the Gaṅgā;

they drank at the river Sarasvatī; / they plunged towards the east!"

"When the village folk and the slave of Māṅgīra / utter malicious words,

either the village prospers in security, / or the draft ox suffers while drawing [the plow]!"

"Here we float, / let the wooden pegs stir about here;

having swallowed the honey for you, / like costus in a dragnet!"
